---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const title = 'Weather & Disaster Disclaimer | Nepal Weather & River Watch Portal';
const description = 'Official disclaimer regarding real-time sensor measurements, weather forecasting probabilities, flood sirens, and mountaineering safety in Nepal.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <!-- Semantic Header -->
  <header class="mb-8">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400 mb-1.5">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-600">Disclaimer</span>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
      <span class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-500 text-white shadow-md shadow-amber-500/20">
        <Icon name="alert-triangle" class="w-5 h-5 text-white" />
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900">
        Hydrometeorological Advisory Disclaimer
      </h1>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-slate-500 mt-1">
      Important operational guidance on automated telemetry, forecast uncertainty, and emergency reliance.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- Content Section -->
  <article class="space-y-6 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
    <section class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-amber-300 bg-amber-50/50 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-amber-950 mb-2">
        1. Automated Remote Telemetry &amp; Sensor Realities
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-amber-900 leading-relaxed">
        Hydrological water level gauges and meteorological automated weather stations (AWS) across Nepal operate in rugged, extreme mountain topographies. Field stations may experience transient data interruptions caused by severe lightning, riverbank silt accumulation, flash flood debris, or solar battery exhaustion during prolonged cloud cover.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-slate-900 mb-3">
        2. Life-Safety &amp; Evacuation Directives
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        This portal is intended for public situational awareness and supplementary disaster preparedness.
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-red-950 font-semibold mb-3">
        Never delay immediate physical evacuation or emergency safety protocols based solely on software readings. When official government sirens sound or district emergency authorities order evacuations, move to higher ground immediately.
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
        Always confirm urgent flood status directly with the Department of Hydrology's 24/7 toll-free emergency hotline at <strong>1155</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-slate-900 mb-3">
        3. High Himalayan Mountaineering &amp; Aviation Flights
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        The High Himalayan mountaineering matrix (3,000m to 9,000m) and Numerical Weather Prediction (NWP) model outputs provide synoptic-scale guidance. High-altitude alpine weather can change drastically within minutes due to localized katabatic winds and valley microclimates.
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600">
        Climbing expedition leaders, trekking guides, and aviation operators must consult certified meteorologists at the Tribhuvan International Airport MFD desk (01-4113191) before undertaking high-altitude summit pushes or mountain flights.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black text-slate-900 mb-3">
        4. No Warranty
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600">
        The information on this website is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranty of any kind, either express or implied, including but not limited to the implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or uninterrupted availability.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
